		Parser for calculator expressions. GENERATED by geyacc from
		grammar/gc_parser.y: edit the grammar, then run scripts/generate_parser.sh.

		Grammar by levels (loosest first): sum, product (with implicit
		multiplication: 2x, 3sin(x), sin(t)e^(-t/4)), signed (unary minus),
		power (right-associative ^), postfix (superscript two), atom. The expression has at most
		one variable: any name that is not a function or a constant (pi, the letter pi, e).
		Unicode operators are written by code point, so geyacc never re-encodes them: middle dot (183)
		and times (215) multiply, minus sign (8722) subtracts, square root (8730), superscript two (178).
